    "details": "Wasmtime development team reports:\n\n> - Wasmtime component async-lifted callback result count is\n>   unvalidated, causing a native stack buffer overflow.\n> - Mis-typed WebAssembly tag imports can lead to GC heap corruption.\n> - Rooting for GC values live across try_call may be missing, causing\n>   GC heap corruption.\n> - Excessive allocated memory on the host when guests don\\'t have\n>   stdio.\n> - Guest can panic host through filesystem timestamp before the epoch\n>   on wasip3.\n> - Wasmtime wasi:http implementation panics with a zero timeout\n>   supplied.\n> - WASI preview 0 implementation of poll_oneoff circumvents fuel\n>   consumption.\n> - fd_readdir copies uninitialized struct padding into guest memory.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0511",
